# CODEOWNERS — moagan
#
# GitHub consults this file when PRs touch the listed paths. The matching
# owner gets auto-assigned and the ruleset can demand their review via
# `pull_request.require_code_owner_review: true` (see docs/branch-protection.md).
#
# Sole maintainer for now (@airvzxf) — the per-area rows exist so we can
# fan out to future co-maintainers without rewriting the file.
#
# Order matters: the last matching rule wins. Keep the most specific
# paths last.

# Default: every file belongs to the project owner.
/.github/                     @airvzxf
/.github/CODEOWNERS           @airvzxf

# Architecture / spec — only the owner can change the normative sources.
# Anything that mutates the architecturally authoritative docs/ requires
# an explicit human review.
/docs/                        @airvzxf
/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md         @airvzxf
/docs/proposal-*.md           @airvzxf
/docs/branch-protection.md    @airvzxf
/docs/validation-tiers.md     @airvzxf

# Build / dependency manifests — touching these is a forced upgrade.
/Cargo.toml                   @airvzxf
/Cargo.lock                   @airvzxf
/lefthook.yml                 @airvzxf
/rustfmt.toml                 @airvzxf
/.clippy.toml                 @airvzxf
/.github/dependabot.yml       @airvzxf

# Source code lives under src/ — owner reviews every PR that touches it.
/src/                         @airvzxf
/tests/                       @airvzxf
/scripts/                     @airvzxf
/Makefile                     @airvzxf

# Everything else still routes to the owner.
*                             @airvzxf
